---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Contact from '../../components/Contact.astro';
import LegalScript from '../../components/LegalScript.astro';
import { operator as o, legalNoticeUrl } from '../../data/legal';
import { url } from '../../lib/paths';
const githubPrivacy = 'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement';
const anthropicPrivacy = 'https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="Privacy policy for the SinnConsulting blog." crumbs={[{ label: 'privacy' }]}>
  <Fragment slot="left">
    <section class="side">
      <h2>Legal</h2>
      <ul class="stack" style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0">
        <li><a href={legalNoticeUrl}>Legal notice (Impressum)</a></li>
        <li><a href={url('privacy/')}>Privacy policy</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="side">
      <h2>In short</h2>
      <p class="muted">No cookies. No tracking. No analytics. Fonts and images are served from this site.</p>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="box"><div class="markdown legal">

    <section lang="en">
      <h1>Privacy <em>policy</em></h1>
      <p class="muted">Datenschutzerklärung</p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>Controller within the meaning of the GDPR:<br /><strong>{o.name}</strong><br />{o.business}<br />
        <Contact kind="address" /><br />Email: <Contact kind="mail" /></p>

      <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
      <p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages. The provider is GitHub Inc., 88 Colin P Kelly Jr St, San Francisco,
        CA 94107, USA. When you visit the website, GitHub automatically collects information in server log files that your
        browser transmits, in particular your IP address, the date and time of access, the page requested and the browser
        used. More information: <a href={githubPrivacy}>GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
      <p>The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR; our legitimate interest is presenting the website reliably. Data is
        transferred to the USA on the basis of the European Commission's adequacy decision under Art. 45 GDPR (EU-US Data
        Privacy Framework), under which GitHub Inc. is certified.</p>

      <h2>3. No cookies, no tracking, no third-party content</h2>
      <p>This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking services. Fonts, images and scripts are loaded only
        from this site; simply reading it sends no data to third parties.</p>
      <p>If you switch to the light theme, that choice is stored in your browser's local storage (localStorage). It never
        leaves your device and is strictly necessary for the feature you asked for (§ 25 (2) no. 2 TDDDG). You can remove it
        at any time with the theme switch or in your browser settings.</p>

      <h2>4. Links to external services</h2>
      <p>Some buttons lead to third-party services. Data is only transmitted once you click such a link; the provider's
        privacy policy then applies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong> (“Suggest edit”, “View source”, “Star on GitHub”, links to commits and repositories):
          GitHub Inc., <a href={githubPrivacy}>privacy statement</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Claude</strong> (“Ask Claude”): opens claude.ai by Anthropic PBC with a prepared question about the post,
          <a href={anthropicPrivacy}>privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>sinn.consulting</strong> (“Legal notice”): our company website, which has its own
          <a href="https://sinn.consulting/privacy.html">privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong>, the <strong>Visual Studio Marketplace</strong> and other linked websites.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Edit suggestions via GitHub</h2>
      <p>If you submit a pull request via “Suggest edit”, you do so from your GitHub account and under GitHub's terms. Your
        GitHub name and your contribution are public there. If the suggestion is merged, your name, the date and the commit
        message appear in the repository's public version history and on the post's “History” page. The legal basis is
        Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (a traceable version history). On request we will remove your name from this website; the
        version history on GitHub cannot always be changed afterwards.</p>

      <h2>6. Contact by email</h2>
      <p>If you contact us by email, we store the details you provide to handle your request and any follow-up questions.
        We do not share them without your consent. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR (pre-contractual measures) or
        Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest). The data is deleted once your request has been fully handled, at the
        latest after three years, unless statutory retention obligations apply.</p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access your stored data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
        <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
        <li>erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
        <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
        <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
        <li>object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. For Bavaria (private
        sector) this is the Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht (BayLDA), Promenade 27, 91522 Ansbach,
        <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de">www.lda.bayern.de</a>.</p>

      <h2>8. Encryption</h2>
      <p>This website is served exclusively over an encrypted connection (HTTPS/TLS).</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {o.updated}</p>
    </section>
  </div></article>
  <LegalScript />
</Base>
